{
  "_doc": "How heroes fight as they level (Systems/Prowess.cs, played out in Systems/Expedition.cs). attacks: the library class feature names that give more weapon attacks a turn; extraAttacks gives classes of our own the levels they gain one. Cantrips roll one more die at each of cantripSteps. Casts are spell slots a long rest (pact magic comes back on a short rest), one number per level 1-20; the highest slot comes from Moments.SpellLevel, and a spell is cast midway between its own level and that. A healer holds keepForHeals casts back for heals, and nobody spends a slot on a damage spell outside a boss fight unless spendFoes foes stand; at most buffs spells steady the party in one fight, and only against a boss or foes with more hit points than the party. spells: the fighting spells, by library id (the library says who knows them, their dice, damage type and save); kind bolt (one foe; beams more rays), blast (area, up to targets foes), heal (one ally, or targets allies), buff (party hit, ac or hp, or haste's extra attack), hold (targets foes save or lose rounds turns: held, or hindered by hit), mark (dice on every hit on one foe), aura (dice to every foe each round for rounds), cantrip. upcast: dice added a slot level above the spell's own. powers: class signature powers, each with the class and level it opens at, uses by level ([level, uses] steps) and the rest that brings them back. damage: what resistance, immunity and vulnerability do; steelVsImmune is what a plain blade does to a creature only magic or silver can hurt. regenRises: times a regenerating creature gets back up in a fight when nothing it fears dropped it. targeting: how foes pick whom to hit by their wits.",
